From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gigi <42325924+g-cqd@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 13:24:38 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Web Extensions: blocking onHeadersReceived holds documents
 only; own flag; headers checked (Sunset W6c)

A held response waits a round trip to the extension: about 0.4 ms a
request with uBlock Origin, measured. Only documents (a frame's main
resource) are held now, where headers decide what the page may do;
subresources go on, and their listeners see them without a say.

Blocking onHeadersReceived listeners have a flag of their own, so an
extension with only a blocking onBeforeRequest listener holds no
responses. Header names must be HTTP tokens and values carry no CR, LF
or NUL (trimmed of spaces); others are dropped. The web process keeps no
set of asked loads: the network process says so on the response
(ResourceLoadInfo), so an aborted load leaves nothing behind.

